                <pb facs="0612" n="513" sameAs="frus:frus1936v02/pg513"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">881.113/33: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Diplomatic Agent and Consul General at
                        Tangier</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Blake</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tangier</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-08-27T17:00:00+00:00">August 27, 1936—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 28—10:15 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>22. Department’s telegraphic instruction No. 11, August 24, 2 p.m.<anchor n="62"
                        xml:id="d447-f1"/> Difficulties foreshadowed in my telegram No. 21, August
                    23, 1 p.m., are arising in acute form. Greatest caution advisable. Am
                    consequently taking no action in matter of acceptance of oil dahir pending
                    developments. Have under consideration and will shortly submit for Department’s
                    approval formula under which dahir may be accepted without any breach of
                    neutrality on our part.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Blake</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
